+// DCS Control (0078): the loop closed, on a model of the layer's pacing in
+// 2X's shape at the shallow depth. Nothing here is the layer's code but the
+// three pieces under test (HandOverBlock, LeaderLead, leader_lead_release);
+// the rest restates, in steps of 50 us, what the live flight of 2026-11-15
+// measured and what openxr_layer.cpp does around them:
+//   the runtime    its wait returns on a grid of display periods, at the
+//                  next point after it is called; its xrEndFrame takes
+//                  0.3 ms, or - a runtime that waits - returns 1.3 ms after
+//                  the submission's output is written
+//   the presenter  one submission a wait, first in first out, 0.3 ms after
+//                  the wait returns, or when the application queues one
+//   the application  `cpu` from its release to its xrEndFrame; its rendering
+//                  is done on the GPU `gpu` later and synthesis `synth`
+//                  after that; admitted once only one submission is
+//                  outstanding; then held until the presenter has run its
+//                  frame's count since the last release, less the lead's
+//                  turns, plus the delay - or at once when the presenter has
+//                  nothing left queued (presenter_starved)
+// With the flight's numbers (90 Hz, cadence 3, 8 ms of CPU, 14.7 ms of
+// rendering, 7.2 ms of synthesis, a release offset of 6.6 ms) the model
+// without the lead reproduces the lock - four periods a frame, the first
+// synthetic written about 14 ms after its hand-over, a slot lost every
+// frame - which is what makes its answer with the lead worth having.
+struct LeadModelResult {
+    double early_periods{};   // mean periods per frame, 0.3-1.0 s
+    double late_periods{};    // mean periods per frame, the last 5 s
+    int late_lost{};          // slots lost in the last 5 s
+    double early_lateness_ms{}; // mean first-synthetic lateness, 0.3-1.0 s
+    double late_lateness_ms{};  // worst in the last 5 s
+    bool latched{};
+    bool ever_latched{};
+    xrfg::latency::Nanoseconds lead{};
+    int raises{};
+};
